Z||000000||TooLowFiero||04-05-2000||06:37 PM||||i have a 86 2m4 that im installing a power trunk release on. I am having problems with it. The Trunk release is from a 84 se and i cannot find the wire or where the wire goes to. is the decklid wired for the trunk release or do i have to splice in somewhere. The dash had the clip and wiring for the release Button but i see nothing in the rear of the car. Please help me out on this.<BR>Thank you in advance<P>TooLow||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||04-05-2000||07:09 PM||||I put a release on my 88 Formula. It was from an older SE (probably 86) in a junkyard. I had to replace the wiring running thru the decklid with the one from the junkyard. <P>There may be another problem with the 84 donor. I believe the 84s "ajar" switch was mounted to the body and later ones had the switch mounted on the latch itself in the decklid. So... the 84 decklid wiring MAY not work. You may need to get the decklid wiring from a newer car or run the wire yourself.<P>BTW, there is also a small relay you need to make it work. The wiring should be there and it mounts under the dash on the right side of the steering column.<P>Hope this helps...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phantom Rage||04-05-2000||08:45 PM||||As always, Orge had a good article about installing a trunk release.  So far I have done two fieros, using his detailed info.  I found it in Orge's Cave.  Sorry I don't remember his site.  Anybody? ||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||04-05-2000||09:11 PM||||  Orges cave hyperlink is located at the bottom of the screen <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000004||theogre||04-05-2000||09:11 PM||||look down............. (the newest way to get there is now on the bottom of every page.)<P>84's wiring is diferant. I don't know if that year even had the remote release. If it did it will be a diferant connector. 84 uses a pin switch on the edge of the trunk for the "ajar" light.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TooLowFiero||04-05-2000||11:04 PM||||thanks you guys for the help.  as you might notice now i use punctuation.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">)  Ogre  i went to your site and found it VERY informative. I will your your opinions and make this thing work. again thatnks for you help guys.  Oh yeah i found another Fiero im gonna pick up. Its an 86 2m4 manual with 86,000 miles on it. all it needs is a clutch(no problem my donor car has a new clutch in it) its in REALLY good condition inside and out and the guy wants 350 for it.  sorry so long <P>thanks a million<P>TooLow||||reg||1
